      "id": "index",
      "name": "Index",
      "category": "TensorIndexList",
      "signature": "Index(Target)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "type2index*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "EIGEN_DEVICE_FUNC operator",
      "docs": "\\internal\n\\class TensorIndexList\n\\ingroup CXX11_Tensor_Module\n\\brief Set of classes used to encode a set of Tensor dimensions/indices.\nThe indices in the list can be known at compile time or at runtime. A mix\nof static and dynamic indices can also be provided if needed. The tensor\ncode will attempt to take advantage of the indices that are known at\ncompile time to optimize the code it generates.\nThis functionality requires a c++11 compliant compiler. If your compiler\nis older you need to use arrays of indices instead.\nSeveral examples are provided in the cxx11_tensor_index_list.cpp file.\n\\sa Tensor",
      "supportedTargets": [
        "type2index*",
        "type2indexpair*"
      ]
    },
